a dramatic and for the short flight from  Izmir to Istanbul the Boeing owned by  Pegasus Airlines was touching down when  pilots appear to have lost control the  plane veered off the runway burst into  flames and broke into pieces  most of the 171 passengers along with  the crew miraculously escaped alive many  suffered injuries and was sent to  hospitals the two pilots reported to be  in a serious condition an investigation  is underway to determine the causes of  the crash Molotov unfortunately the  Pegasus Airlines plane could not stay on  the runway due to poor weather  conditions and skidded for around 50 to  60 meters it fell from 30 to 40 meters  175 passengers two babies for flight  attendants and two pilots were on board  120 passengers have so far been  transferred to nearby hospitals there  was a thunderstorm bringing gusty winds  at the time of the incident the  authorities closed the airport and  diverted flights to different  destinations this isn't the first time  Pigasus has been involved in such an  incident two years ago one of its Jets  skidded off the runway at Robson Airport  and ended up halfway down a steep slope  by the Black Sea all 162 passengers and  crew aboard were evacuated safely  Pegasus Airlines is likely to face  further scrutiny in the coming days last  month one of its planes slid off the  runway at Sabiha gökçen Airport  investigators said the incident was due  to bad weather conditions  Hoshi Mohammed Al Jazeera Istanbul
 

